{"author":{"id":"673e1e1b6fccff4da5524407c8a8cdc7caf18221aabb93f2bb36ffef5c2a95e8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781331245,"nonce":"L/dctORXfh8IUNESiJY1eUnmiX0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABFW8ohw","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/17","origin":"github"},"title":"Spot bid is locked at pool create and never re-evaluated","message":"The bid is computed once in `chooseBidPrice` at `Create` and never revisited. `IsDrifted` is a deliberate no-op, so a pool whose locked bid falls below a rising market is only corrected by preemption.\n\n### Evidence\n- `pkg/cloudprovider/cloudprovider.go:68-75` `IsDrifted` returns `\"\", nil`, commenting that \"the bid is locked at pool create time.\"\n- `pkg/providers/instance/instance.go:261` `chooseBidPrice` runs only on the Create path.\n\n### Impact\nIf market price climbs above the locked bid, the node is preempted; recovery happens only when Karpenter creates a **new** NodeClaim (new UID → new pool → re-bid at current market). It self-heals, but disruptively and reactively — there is no proactive re-bid or drift signal as the market moves.\n\n### Suggested fix (options)\n- Implement `IsDrifted` to flag pools whose locked bid is below current market (or below market × factor), letting Karpenter roll them proactively; **or**\n- A periodic reconciler that patches `BidPrice` on existing pools toward current market (if Rackspace permits in-place bid updates — confirm via the SDK pool Update path).\n- Either way, document the trade-off chosen (proactive churn vs. reactive preemption).","files":null}]}